In the system of equations shown,  c  is a constant.
 \begin{cases} y = \frac{3}{4}x - 2 \\ 9x - cy = 24 \end{cases} 
If the system has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of  c ?

In the system of equations shown,  a  is a constant.
 \begin{cases} 3x - 8y = 12 \\ (a-2)x - 24y = 36 \end{cases} 
If the system has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of  a ?

In the system of equations shown,  c  is a constant.
 \begin{cases} 6x - 8y = 3 \\ 9x + cy = 5 \end{cases} 
If the system has no solution, what is the value of  c ?
